#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0660 expect=violation domain=FT
#note "S1 (2026-09-14): the pin moved from variable_name to the RESOLVED column, because the Check moved from varname() per-variable iteration to var_exists(\"--EVAL\") / var_exists(\"--EVALID\"). The -- prefix resolves to the current domain, so this rule can no longer cross-match a foreign-domain column (a stray FTEVAL in a QS dataset used to satisfy the old hard-coded membership list). The SECOND member of the membership list: an FT dataset declaring FTEVALID (QSEVALID absent) -> one finding pinned by variable_name=FTEVALID. The retired CORE-family twin covered only the QS name, so this is the one place FTEVALID is exercised at all."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 nameOnly=FTEVALID
dataset FT label="Functional Tests"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col FTSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col FTEVALID type=Char label="Evaluator Identifier"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | FT | 01-701-1015 | 1 | RATER01
